-- title:
--   A twist of δ with regular elliptic rational norm
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a $K$-algebra of degree $\operatorname{finrank}_K L = 2$, and let $\sigma : L \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K]} L$ be such that every $K$-automorphism $\tau$ of $L$ lies in the subgroup generated by the integer powers of $\sigma$. Let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$, write $K_v$ for the $v$-adic completion, let $c$ be a unit of $K_v$, and let $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$. Assume (i) the scalar matrix with diagonal entry $c$, viewed in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$, is a norm of $\delta$ in the sense of [`AutomorphicForm.IsNormOf`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L217), i.e. its image under `toTensorGL` equals $y^{-1}\,(\mathrm{normString}\ \delta)\,y$ for some $y \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$, and (ii) for no unit $z$ of $L \otimes_K K_v$ is $\delta$ $\sigma$-conjugate to the scalar matrix of $z$, $\sigma$-conjugacy meaning that the scalar equals $x^{-1}\delta\,\sigma(x)$ for some $x \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$, where $\sigma$ acts through `sigmaGL`, the entrywise application of `sigmaTensor`. Then there exist $u_0$ in the twisted centraliser of $\delta$, that is satisfying $u_0\,\delta\,\sigma(u_0)^{-1} = \delta$, and $\gamma_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ such that $\operatorname{tr}(\gamma_0)^2 - 4\det(\gamma_0)$ is a unit of $K_v$ (the predicate [`AutomorphicForm.IsRegularSemisimple`](def/AutomorphicForm_LocalOrbitalBase.html#L402)) and is not a square in $K_v$, and $\gamma_0$ is a norm of $u_0\delta$ in the above sense.
--
--   This is the existence, in the twisted orbital setting for a quadratic extension of number fields at a finite place, of a twist $u_0\delta$ of $\delta$ whose norm can be taken to be a regular element of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ with non-square discriminant, hence elliptic; it is the local analogue of Langlands' lemma on $\sigma$-conjugacy classes with $\sigma$-stable norm for $\mathrm{GL}(2)$. It provides the reference norm pair away from the centre used by [`AutomorphicForm.exists_ellipticTransport_coupled_straighten_of_not_isSigmaConjugate_scalar_of_finrank_eq_two`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_ellipticTransport_coupled_straighten_of_not_isSigmaConjugate_scalar_of_finrank_eq_two) in the comparison of twisted and ordinary orbital integrals.
